+
+## Verification commands and outputs
+
+- `test -f daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/identity/serialization.rs`
+  - `OK`
+- `test -f daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/identity_payload.rs`
+  - `OK`
+- `cd daemon && cargo build --release`
+  - `Finished 'release' profile [optimized] target(s) in 2m 05s`
+- `cd daemon && cargo test --workspace -- identity::serialization`
+  - `5 passed; 0 failed`
+  - Tests run:
+    - `identity::serialization::tests::not_found_outcome_is_truthful`
+    - `identity::serialization::tests::legacy_name_is_preserved`
+    - `identity::serialization::tests::compact_form_round_trips`
+    - `identity::serialization::tests::structured_form_is_accepted`
+    - `identity::serialization::tests::ambiguity_payload_shape_is_structured`
+- `cd daemon && cargo test --workspace -- rpc::identity_payload`
+  - `2 passed; 0 failed`
+  - Tests run:
+    - `rpc::identity_payload::tests::ambiguous_resolver_outcome_surfaces_diagnostic`
+    - `rpc::identity_payload::tests::full_tool_response_includes_identity_payloads_and_legacy_fields`
+- `wc -l daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/identity/serialization.rs daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/identity_payload.rs`
+  - `319 daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/identity/serialization.rs`
+  - `505 daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/identity_payload.rs`
+  - `824 total`
+- `rg -n "TODO|FIXME|XXX" daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/identity/serialization.rs daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/identity_payload.rs daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/context_cache.rs daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/mcp.rs docs/architecture/2026-05-16-mcp-compatibility-policy.md`
+  - No matches
+
+## Issues encountered
+
+- The first implementation tried to use `IdentityResolver` directly against the `get_context_capsule` in-memory graph and relative file paths. That produced `not_found` outcomes because the resolver expects workspace-qualified stored paths for this code path. I fixed it by keeping the core `serialize_outcome(...)` contract, but deriving the resolver-compatible `ResolveOutcome` directly from the live graph for this representative MCP payload wrapper. That preserved ambiguity diagnostics without changing unrelated resolver behavior.
+
+## Final status
+
+`complete`

